# Generated artifact — bluebook-of-record :
#   aggregates/framework/mindstream/mindstream.bluebook (Mindstream, MindstreamMember types)
#   aggregates/framework/mindstream/mindstream.fixtures (the boot Mindstream + its boot member)
#
# Until the :overmind generator capability lands (i262), this file is
# hand-derived from those two bluebooks and committed as if it were
# generated. To regenerate manually : read mindstream.fixtures, list
# every MindstreamMember whose lifespan.kind=="one_shot" in
# OVERMIND_CAN_DIE, then add the framework env (HECKS_DAEMON, etc.)
# the boot pipeline needs.

OVERMIND_CAN_DIE=boot
HECKS_DAEMON=1

# Persistence cutover ROLLED BACK (2026-06-14) : the env-var cutover created a
# split-brain — the MCP door (Claude Code's inherited env) wrote OLD while these
# daemons wrote ~/.heki/miette, splitting Miette's memory aggregates across two
# stores. Rolled daemons back to the single OLD store. The ~/.heki/miette rsync
# copy stays as the de-risked backup. The real cutover lands later as the
# STRUCTURAL change (persistence plan step D : resolve_info_dir default →
# ~/.heki/<deployment> + .world config, no env-var reliance — env-var routing is
# exactly what caused the split-brain). No HECKS_INFO override here ; daemons
# resolve to the miette-state sibling, same store as the door.
